Born in the flooded, corrugated-iron under-bridges of the South Sub-Level districts, Monsoon Foundry is the soundtrack of scrap-metal salvagers and midnight circuit-benders. Originating from the underground pirate transmissions of the defunct "Station 9-Gale," this subculture dresses in waterproof, salt-stained denim patched with blinking fiber-optic ribbons and heavy steel-toe boots designed to trudge through knee-deep oily floodwater. Their rituals involve gathering beneath highway overpasses during high-voltage squalls, plugging acoustic instruments straight into discarded power grid terminals, and dancing until the circuitry fries.

